[medium] LICENSE:1 (correctness)
The branch replaces the repository license text from GNU AGPLv3 to Apache-2.0. That is a substantive relicensing of the whole policy bundle, not a policy implementation change, and there is no accompanying approval or metadata update proving the project has permission to relicense existing code. Pushing this as-is can make downstream use and distribution legally incorrect.
Suggested fix: Restore the existing AGPLv3 LICENSE text unless the relicensing is intentional and approved; if intentional, include the explicit approval/context and update any related project metadata in the same change.
Guidance: In LICENSE, restore the repository's prior GNU AGPLv3 license text unless there is explicit project-owner approval to relicense this bundle to Apache-2.0. Do not leave a partial license header or mix AGPL and Apache text. If relicensing is actually intentional and approved, keep Apache-2.0 only with that approval documented in the change and update any related metadata or README license references in the same commit; otherwise, the safe fix is to revert LICENSE exactly to the previous AGPLv3 contents from the base branch.
