[low] Makefile:5 (test quality)
The changed `validate` target now runs `opa check policies` while README and CI both require `opa check --strict policies`. This makes the local validation command weaker than the documented and enforced check, so contributors can miss strict-mode Rego issues until CI.
Suggested fix: Change the Makefile target back to `opa check --strict policies` so local validation, README instructions, and CI all execute the same check.
Guidance: In Makefile, update the validate target command from `@opa check policies` to `@opa check --strict policies` so local validation matches README.md and .github/workflows/test.yml. Keep the target name and help text unchanged. Do not change the test target or replace validate with opa fmt/opa test; the specific missing behavior is strict Rego checking.
